      <section>
        {/* 표제는 원문 '제3자 청구에 대한 방어'를 그대로 옮긴다. 'Indemnification'으로 부르면 제3자 지식재산권
            청구로 한정된 이 조가 일반적인 손해 보전 약속처럼 넓게 읽힐 수 있다(용어집 §4 · §11 넓어진 곳). */}
        <h2>Article 23 (Defense Against Third-Party Claims)</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>If the Customer receives a claim from a third party alleging that the Service infringes the third party’s intellectual property rights in the Republic of Korea, the Company will defend the claim at its own expense and bear the damages the Customer is ordered to pay under a final and binding judgment. However, this applies only if the Customer notifies the Company without delay and cooperates in the defense.</li>
          <li>
            In the case of paragraph (1), the Company may, at its option, take any of the following measures:
            <ul>
              <li>Securing the right to continue using the Service</li>
              <li>Modifying the Service so that it no longer infringes</li>
              <li>Terminating the Individual Agreement and refunding the Fees for the remaining term</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>If a third party’s rights are infringed due to Customer Data or the Customer’s instructions, the Customer will defend and indemnify the Company in the same manner.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Article 24 (Assignment of Rights and Obligations)</h2>
        <p>Neither the Company nor the Customer may assign to a third party, or provide as collateral, its rights or obligations under these Terms and the Individual Agreement without the other party’s prior written consent. However, this does not apply to universal succession resulting from a merger, division, or business transfer, in which case the relevant party will notify the other party without delay.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Article 25 (Notices)</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Notices from the Company to the Customer take effect when sent to the email address stated in the Individual Agreement.</li>
          <li>Notices to Users in general may instead be given by posting on the Website. However, the Company will notify the Customer individually of matters that materially affect the Customer’s rights or obligations.</li>
          <li>If the Customer’s contact information changes, the Customer must notify the Company without delay, and the Company is not responsible for any disadvantage arising from the Customer’s failure to do so.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section>
